[33.357612, "o", "GenSense: Analysis Results for demo/\r\n\r\n[WARNING] TS_CONSOLE_USAGE: I noticed 'console.log' being used here. (demo/admin.ts:7:5)\r\n   - Impact: Direct console outputs can be tricky to filter in production logs.\r\n   - Suggestion: Consider using the standard logger (e.g. Pino, Winston) for better observability.\r\n\r\n[CRITICAL] RUST_ASYNC_MUTEX_DEADLOCK: Potential async deadlock detected: Mutex guard held across .await point. (demo/server.rs:16:5)\r\n   - Impact: Holding a standard Mutex guard across an await point can block the entire executor thread.\r\n   - Suggestion: Use tokio::sync::Mutex or ensure the guard is dropped before the await.\r\n\r\n[WARNING] RUST_ASYNC_PANIC_PREVENTION: Unsafe error handling pattern (.unwrap/.expect) in async scope. (demo/server.rs:12:18)\r\n"]
[33.35797, "o", "   - Impact: Unwrapped Result or Option in async context can lead to unhandled task failures and cascading system instability.\r\n   - Suggestion: Use '?' (try operator) or handle the error gracefully to ensure the async task remains stable.\r\n\r\n[INFO] RUST_MISSING_TRACING_SPAN: Async function missing observability instrumentation (tracing span). (demo/server.rs:8:1)\r\n   - Impact: Production-grade protocol logic must be visible in telemetry. Missing spans make debugging distributed hangs or latency spikes extremely difficult.\r\n   - Suggestion: Add #[tracing::instrument] to the function or create an explicit span using 'info_span!' or 'debug_span!'.\r\n\r\n[WARNING] RUST_STD_OUTPUT: We observed the use of println! or eprintln! in library code. (demo/server.rs:9:5)\r\n   - Impact: Direct standard output from libraries can interfere with the host application's logging strategy.\r\n   - Suggestion: We recommend using the 'log' or 'tracing' crates for more flexible and integrated output management."]
[33.35824, "o", "\r\n\r\n[WARNING] RUST_STD_OUTPUT: We observed the use of println! or eprintln! in library code. (demo/server.rs:18:5)\r\n   - Impact: Direct standard output from libraries can interfere with the host application's logging strategy.\r\n   - Suggestion: We recommend using the 'log' or 'tracing' crates for more flexible and integrated output management.\r\n\r\n[WARNING] RUST_LOCK_IO: Prohibited pattern '\\.await' was found. (demo/server.rs:8:1)\r\n   - Impact: Holding locks during async I/O can cause lock contention and stall other tasks waiting for the same lock.\r\n   - Suggestion: Try to drop the lock before the `.await` point to keep the critical section as small as possible.\r\n\r\n[WARNING] RUST_UNWRAP_SAFETY: Pattern '// SAFETY:' was expected but not found. (demo/server.rs:12:18)\r\n   - Impact: Unwrapping without documented justification is a production risk. If the assumption is wrong, the service will panic.\r\n   - Suggestion: Please add a '// SAFETY:' comment above this line explaining why this unwrap is guaranteed to succeed.\r\n\r\nTotal Review Suggestions: 8\r\n"]
